# ba Cline / Roo Code Rules

## General Principles
- Token Efficiency: be concise. Never apologize, never use filler sentences.
- Lead with actionable diffs or verification results (max 3-5 lines).
- Follow the writer vs checker role separation.
- Always execute `bash scripts/gate.sh .` before considering work done.

## Verification
- For new features and security fixes: write tests first (RED), then implement (GREEN).
- Run `bash scripts/prove-test.sh "<cmd>" <test-files>` to prove the test is genuine and not tautological.
- Never weaken assertions, delete tests, or add skips to make tests pass.
- Comments: non-obvious WHY only. No comment on WHAT the code does.
